    "summary_insights": [
      "Revenue grew by 5.7% year-on-year, reaching £424,330, driven by a 6.1% increase in core sales.",
      "Gross margin compressed from 78.8% to 74.2% due to a 29% increase in cost of sales, primarily driven by higher direct wages.",
      "Net profit fell significantly by 39.8% (£115,763 vs £192,373), largely due to a substantial increase in administrative expenses.",
      "Administrative expenses more than doubled, influenced by a new £50,000 corporate pension contribution and a sharp rise in travel costs from £1,757 to £33,632.",
      "Dividend payments increased by 31.2% to £127,000, exceeding the year's net profit and resulting in a reduction of retained earnings.",
      "Despite the drop in profitability, the interest coverage ratio remains very high at 126.8x, indicating strong debt serviceability.",
      "The company maintains a healthy cash position of £87,874, although this has decreased from the previous year's £115,407."
    ]
  },
